%N A398603 a(n) is the least number which is the end of an arithmetic progression of n numbers that are the sums of two squares (A001481).
%C A398603 Conjecture: a(n) = A093365(n) for n >= 13.
%e A398603 a(12) = 961 is the end of the arithmetic progression 37, 121, 205, 289, 373, 457, 541, 625, 709, 793, 877, 961 with steps A398604(12) = 84. The continuation of the progression 961 + 84 = 1045 is not a term of A001481. No 12-term progression with smaller end exists.
%Y A398603 A398604 are the corresponding steps.
%Y A398603 Cf. A093365, A093366 (similar, but for A000404 instead of A001481).
